  "lineage": "Mapuche ülkantun (\"singing\") sung-poetry tradition of the Mapuche communities of southern Argentina and central-southern Chile, distinct from the more specialized tayil women's genealogical-ritual chant. The ülkantun encompasses the broader Mapuche song-repertoire spanning everyday-occasion songs, mourning-laments, war-songs, courtship-songs, and political-resistance songs. Performance: solo singer often accompanying themselves on kultrun shallow-frame-drum (the canonical Mapuche ceremonial-percussion-instrument), with characteristic narrow-range Mapuche pentatonic melodic vocabulary and the Mapudungun language base. The post-1990 Chilean-democratic-transition cultural-revival under the Mapuche cultural-policy organizations consolidated institutional visibility; the Mapuche post-2010 political-mobilization period has reinvigorated the genre.",
